                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Crazy Car is an expensive racing game that doesn't offer anything besides four colours and four cars, while the cars look different and offer slightly better stats compared to the starter, overall the game and everything in it is not worth the price tag that, at one point, was apparently $200 dollars.\n\nMost of the negative reviews seem to be from the developer revoking keys and generally being an overall terrible person, but the game itself is just as bad. It offers very little except four achievements that can be painfully tedious to get if you decide to race around the one and only track multiple times (or simply find a long pathway, which first appears roughtly 2,000 metres(?) in then reverse about 500 metres(?) then repeat give or take 400 times, which is what I did, took me 90ish minutes. \nThe only reason I can think of to get this game is as an achievement hunter, but even then I strongly recommend not getting it. There are far, far cheaper games that offer much more, spend your money on those more deserving games.",
